{"title":"2012 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 1a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.5</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Adam and Budan are playing a game of Bocce. Each wants their ball to land closest to the jack ball. The positions of Adam’s ball, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, Budan's ball, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and the jack ball, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> are shown in the diagram.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the distance from A to J?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/9/a59b9a6c6724df7384848b8ea1772a120b9e2652.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AJ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" />, the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, is the hypotenuse of the right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/689c69ffdb9b9ccf35ed06a10c793abfe5e19d71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APJ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/1/f918c693a81ce6e14fe9a469a254a7901cbdbf60.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] dot((0,0)); label(&quot;A&quot;,(0,0),S); dot((20,15)); draw((0,0)--(20,15)); label(&quot;J&quot;,(20,15),E); label(&quot;&quot;,(0,0)--(20,15),SE); dot((20,0)); draw((0,0)--(20,0)); label(&quot;20&quot;,(0,0)--(20,0),S); label(&quot;15&quot;,(20,0)--(20,15),E); label(&quot;P&quot;,(20,0),S); draw((20,0)--(20,15)); draw((19,1)--(20,1)); draw((19,0)--(19,1)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"192\" />\n(only right triangle APJ: AP = 20, PJ = 15, AJ = hypotenuse, and angle APJ is the right angle)\n</p><p>Since triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/689c69ffdb9b9ccf35ed06a10c793abfe5e19d71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APJ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> is a right triangle, we can use the Pythagorean theorem to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/9/a59b9a6c6724df7384848b8ea1772a120b9e2652.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AJ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/3/943a6b45bedf8d01a7fab3c129fb5eecff3eafed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP^{2} + PJ^{2} = AJ^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7cca9021b3076f2232a6231c8fac8530a36f6a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AJ = \\sqrt{AP^{2} + PJ^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"158\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f40ac57b8c09b71b11614617919b54bd4aee4544.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/1/4b177b7b2045da4118bb4d36c99eebd75c82cf36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PJ = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a0791a9c74e2530cda5a021e682dd218a4137f09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AJ = \\sqrt{20^{2} + 15^{2}} = \\sqrt{400 + 225}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"256\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/8/a58006a400d1727a026bb10ff81cf17f2ea0f4b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\sqrt{625} = \\boxed{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"117\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.5\">Solution 1.5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the same triangle as solution 1 to find the hypotenuse, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/9/a59b9a6c6724df7384848b8ea1772a120b9e2652.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AJ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/1/f918c693a81ce6e14fe9a469a254a7901cbdbf60.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] dot((0,0)); label(&quot;A&quot;,(0,0),S); dot((20,15)); draw((0,0)--(20,15)); label(&quot;J&quot;,(20,15),E); label(&quot;&quot;,(0,0)--(20,15),SE); dot((20,0)); draw((0,0)--(20,0)); label(&quot;20&quot;,(0,0)--(20,0),S); label(&quot;15&quot;,(20,0)--(20,15),E); label(&quot;P&quot;,(20,0),S); draw((20,0)--(20,15)); draw((19,1)--(20,1)); draw((19,0)--(19,1)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"192\" />\n(only right triangle APJ: AP = 20, PJ = 15, AJ = hypotenuse, and angle APJ is the right angle)\n</p><p>However, instead of using the Pythagorean theorem, we can realize or notice that the sides of the right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/689c69ffdb9b9ccf35ed06a10c793abfe5e19d71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APJ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times the length of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> right triangle because both are right triangles and there are legs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/0/b5057bf2019dff57333d3a5fa04c8fa4468a5426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AJ = 5 \\times 5 = \\boxed{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"146\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017230529\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 123/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1063/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5318/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.564      1 2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%   13.564      1 -total\n 40.72%    5.523      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35638:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017230529 and revision id 279119. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}